{"task":{"id":"Prob137_fsm_serial","spec":"
I would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following
interface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise
specified.

 - input  clk
 - input  reset
 - input  in
 - output done

In many (older) serial communications protocols, each data byte is sent
along with a start bit and a stop bit, to help the receiver delimit bytes
from the stream of bits. One common scheme is to use one start bit (0), 8
data bits, and 1 stop bit (1). The line is also at logic 1 when nothing
is being transmitted (idle).

Implement a finite state machine that will identify when bytes have been
correctly received when given a stream of bits. It needs to identify the
start bit, wait for all 8 data bits, then verify that the stop bit was
correct. If the stop bit does not appear when expected, the FSM must wait
until it finds a stop bit before attempting to receive the next byte.
Include a active-high synchronous reset. Note that the serial protocol
sends the least significant bit first.

Assume all sequential logic is triggered on the positive edge of the
clock.

","interface":{"top":"TopModule","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"reset","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"in","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"done","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."},"current":{"revision_id":"7c9d71c6-596e-4abb-831c-7fe68d75c71c","source_sha256":"56154655cd86d555c80a174b68b88f507c6ea327fca62bdd4bb298ca97ecef87","source":"module TopModule (
    input  clk,
    input  reset,
    input  in,
    output done
);

    localparam [2:0] IDLE = 3'd0,
                     DATA = 3'd1,
                     STOP = 3'd2,
                     DONE = 3'd3,
                     WAIT = 3'd4;

    reg [2:0] state;
    reg [3:0] bit_cnt;

    // Strictly one cycle per received bit: the start bit is recognised in IDLE,
    // and the very next clock edge is data bit 0.  Hence no extra waiting state
    // is used, otherwise the stop-bit check would occur one cycle too late.
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset) begin
            state   <= IDLE;
            bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
        end else begin
            case (state)
                IDLE: begin
                    bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                    if (!in)
                        state <= DATA;     // start bit (0) detected
                end
                DATA: begin
                    if (bit_cnt == 4'd7) begin
                        state   <= STOP;   // all 8 data bits consumed
                        bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                    end else begin
                        bit_cnt <= bit_cnt + 4'd1;
                    end
                end
                STOP: begin
                    // good stop bit (1) -> byte complete; otherwise resync
                    state <= in ? DONE : WAIT;
                end
                DONE: begin
                    bit_cnt <= 4'd0;
                    // current bit is either idle or the next start bit
                    state <= in ? IDLE : DATA;
                end
                WAIT: begin
                    // hunt for a stop bit before receiving the next byte
                    state <= in ? IDLE : WAIT;
                end
                default: state <= IDLE;
            endcase
        end
    end

    assign done = (state == DONE);

endmodule
"},"previous_tool_result":{"tool":"edit_dut","accepted":true,"observation":{"revision_id":"7c9d71c6-596e-4abb-831c-7fe68d75c71c","source_sha256":"56154655cd86d555c80a174b68b88f507c6ea327fca62bdd4bb298ca97ecef87","verification_state":"UNVERIFIED","test_suite_id":"Prob137_fsm_serial"}},"verification_key":null,"observed":null,"repair_control":{"mode":"normal","compacted":false,"best_revision_id":"f6605d76-2940-487c-be6e-8b62e8fed7ed","best_source_sha256":"5636d6627a8ce5bd410f0203500cce1e3a18e4d19bdda34bb9228208442f7a1c","rejected":[{"revision_id":"71e94d16-51c7-49aa-be72-82494b3dd5c9","source_sha256":"54f7d6343c37f67b0e65b691cb9b48c7e3f701777d6dbbeec28ef60a0e698065","reason":"NO_IMPROVEMENT","checks":905,"mismatches":64}]},"repair_ledger":[{"task_id":"Prob137_fsm_serial","sample_id":"ca8e2830-db85-4711-b15a-4d3a1adf32e2","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"f6605d76-2940-487c-be6e-8b62e8fed7ed","source_sha256":"5636d6627a8ce5bd410f0203500cce1e3a18e4d19bdda34bb9228208442f7a1c","verification_key":"sha256:a6d5ab118b22316f3b28f5a8580bbffb264cbe51324376a250c4bdfade67d58a","stage":"simulation","status":"FAIL","checks":905,"mismatches":64},{"task_id":"Prob137_fsm_serial","sample_id":"ca8e2830-db85-4711-b15a-4d3a1adf32e2","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"71e94d16-51c7-49aa-be72-82494b3dd5c9","source_sha256":"54f7d6343c37f67b0e65b691cb9b48c7e3f701777d6dbbeec28ef60a0e698065","verification_key":"sha256:fe256e2e5b453b52aa13537a78252ffc1a87802ecb967862e5bf5b7a33eb0f33","stage":"simulation","status":"FAIL","checks":905,"mismatches":64}],"action_instruction":"Continue from the best verified observation. Rejected revisions were restored; try a different repair. Waveform samples are observations, not proven causes.","verification_state":"UNVERIFIED","history":[{"task_id":"Prob137_fsm_serial","sample_id":"ca8e2830-db85-4711-b15a-4d3a1adf32e2","variant_id":"C","revision_id":"f6605d76-2940-487c-be6e-8b62e8fed7ed","source_sha256":"5636d6627a8ce5bd410f0203500cce1e3a18e4d19bdda34bb9228208442f7a1c"